.TH OCCLUVIEW 1 "August 2026" "OccluView" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
occluview \- advanced Mesh Repair and Mesh Editing for dental CAD
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B occluview
.RI [ OPTION ] [ FILE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
OccluView is an advanced dental CAD workspace for Mesh Repair and Mesh Editing.
It opens STL, PLY, OBJ, GLB, and supported HPS mesh files in an interactive
desktop viewport. Additional files passed to a running instance are added to
its current scene.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.BR \-V , " " \-\-version
Show the installed version.
.TP
.B \-\-diagnostics
Run a no-window graphics adapter and device check, write a diagnostic report,
and exit. This does not prove that the current desktop can create a GUI
surface. The report is stored below the OccluView state directory.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/doc/occluview/
contains usage, license, and third-party attribution documents.
.PP
On Linux, reports are stored below
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/OccluView/
when that variable is set, otherwise below
.I $HOME/.local/state/OccluView/.
Windows stores them below the user's application state directory.
Crash reports are in the
.I crashes/
subdirectory; the metadata-only
.I startup-journal.log
file records the last reached startup boundary when a native driver failure
happens before a crash report can be written.
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
If the viewer exits before opening a window, run
.B occluview --diagnostics
from a terminal and attach the resulting report. The package cannot supply a
missing vendor GPU driver or a broken desktop session.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR occluview-cli (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/occlutrace/OccluView/issues.
